UPDATE companies SET description='Renu Energy Solutions was founded in 2010 in Charlotte, North Carolina, as a locally owned solar installation company serving North and South Carolina. The firm operates regional offices across the Southeast.

The company provides turn-key solar energy system installations for residential and commercial customers, including energy storage, EV charging, and system monitoring. All installations are performed by in-house W2 employees rather than subcontractors. Renu holds both general contractor and electrical contractor licenses, and its staff includes NABCEP-certified professionals. To date, the company has completed over 6,000 solar installations and more than 1,500 energy storage installations across the Southeast.

Renu serves homeowners, businesses, nonprofits, and municipalities throughout the Carolinas and the broader Southeast. Commercial clients range from small businesses to corporations, and the company manages utility interconnection processes such as Duke Energy''s PowerPair program. Residential projects include custom-designed solar arrays, battery backup systems from brands like Tesla Powerwall, FranklinWH, and Generac, and whole-home standby generators.

Renu differentiates itself through a fully integrated, in-house model that handles design, permitting, utility applications, and installation under one roof. The company cites its policy of adjusting customer contracts when material costs decrease as an example of its commitment to transparency. Licensing, certification, and direct employment of installers are presented as the foundation of consistent quality and accountability.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP Certified Employees','Licensed General Contractor','Licensed Electrical Contractor']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design and installation", "Battery energy storage installation", "EV charging station installation", "Solar system monitoring and maintenance", "Standby generator installation", "Permitting and utility interconnection management", "Commercial solar installation", "Residential solar installation", "Nonprofit and municipal solar installation"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Nonprofit solar", "Municipal solar", "Energy storage", "EV charging infrastructure", "Backup power generation"], "materials": ["Solar panels (CertainTeed, Hyundai, Silfab, Tesla)", "Inverters (SolarEdge, Enphase)", "Battery storage (Tesla Powerwall 3, SolarEdge Nexis, Franklin aPower S, Generac PWRCell2)", "Generators (Generac)"], "equipment": ["CertainTeed solar panels", "Hyundai solar panels", "Silfab solar panels", "Tesla solar panels", "SolarEdge inverters", "Enphase microinverters", "Tesla Powerwall 3", "SolarEdge Nexis", "Franklin aPower S", "Generac PWRCell2", "Generac standby generators"], "volume": "Over 6,000 solar installations; over 1,500 energy storage installations", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house employee (W2) installers, not subcontractors", "NABCEP certified employees", "Licensed general contractor and electrical contractor", "Turn-key service including permitting and utility applications", "Contract price adjustments when material costs drop"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2010 -> db", "Headquarters Charlotte, NC -> db", "Locally owned -> /about", "In-house W2 installers -> /about", "Over 6,000 solar installations -> /about", "Over 1,500 energy storage installations -> /about", "NABCEP certified employees -> /about", "Licensed general contractor -> /about", "Licensed electrical contractor -> /about", "Turn-key service including permitting -> /about", "Serves residential, commercial, nonprofit, municipal -> /about", "Brands installed: CertainTeed, Hyundai, Silfab, Tesla panels -> /", "Inverters: SolarEdge, Enphase -> /", "Batteries: Tesla Powerwall 3, SolarEdge Nexis, Franklin aPower S, Generac PWRCell2 -> /", "Generators: Generac -> /", "Duke Energy PowerPair program -> /about", "Contract price adjustment when material costs drop -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Renu Energy Solutions is a locally owned solar installer serving North and South Carolina since 2010.", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='renu-energy-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Republic Wire Inc. began operations in Cincinnati, Ohio, in January 1982. Founder Ron Rosenbeck, who had been in the copper industry since 1973, started the company in a 3,000-square-foot warehouse. The business remains under his ownership as CEO.

The company manufactures a range of copper and aluminum wiring products, including bare copper, THHN, XHHW, USE, NM-B, TFFN, TW, polyweatherproof, tinned copper, PV, UF, MHF, URD, SER, SEU, and aluminum variants. Production uses electrolytically refined 99% pure copper insulated with polyvinyl chloride, with in-line testing for imperfections. The operation now occupies a 350,000-square-foot modern production facility in West Chester Township, Ohio.

Republic Wire serves electrical wholesale distributors, utility distributors, Rural Utilities Service (RUS) cooperatives, investor-owned utilities, and municipalities nationwide. Its product line is designed to meet the needs of these customer segments with an emphasis on inventory availability and fill rates.

The company was founded on principles of customer service, hard work, and loyalty, with a commitment to delivering high-quality products on time. Republic Wire emphasizes its USA manufacturing and a team-based approach to quality and service.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Copper wire drawing and stranding", "Aluminum wire drawing", "Bare copper wire manufacturing", "Insulated building wire manufacturing (THHN, THW, XHHW, USE, NM-B, TFFN, TW)", "Polyweatherproof wire manufacturing", "Tinned copper wire manufacturing", "Electrolytic copper refining (99% purity)", "PVC insulation extrusion", "In-line inspection and testing"], "industries": ["Electrical wholesale distributors", "Utility distributors", "Rural Utilities Service (RUS) cooperatives", "Investor-owned utilities", "Municipalities"], "materials": ["Copper (99% pure electrolytic)", "Aluminum", "Polyvinyl chloride (PVC)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All copper wire products manufactured in the USA", "Extensive inventory for speed, accuracy, and fill rate", "Team-based approach to quality assurance", "Responsive customer service with low-cost emphasis"], "facts_used": ["Founded in January 1982 -> /about-us", "Founder Ron Rosenbeck, owner and CEO -> /about-us", "Started in 3,000 sq ft warehouse in Cincinnati -> /about-us", "Facility now 350,000 sq ft modern production facility -> /about-us", "Manufactures copper and aluminum wire products -> /", "Product list includes bare copper, THHN, XHHW, USE, NM-B, TFFN, TW, polyweatherproof, tinned copper, PV, UF, MHF, URD, SER, SEU, aluminum variants -> /", "Serves electrical wholesale distributors, utility distributors, RUS, investor-owned utilities, municipalities -> /about-us", "All copper wire products manufactured in the USA -> /", "Team concept at RWI for quality assurance -> /about-us", "Electrolytically refined high grade copper, 99% pure -> /", "Polyvinyl chloride insulation with cooling and in-line testing -> /", "Headquarters West Chester Township, Ohio -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Republic Wire originally manufactured top-quality bare copper wire", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='republic-wire-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Revere Plastics Systems operates a manufacturing facility in Ankeny, Iowa, as part of a company headquartered in Novi, Michigan. With over 50 years of experience in plastics manufacturing, the business has spent more than 25 years ranked among the top 100 injection molders in North America. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure, and no founders are named in public materials.

The Ankeny site provides value-added plastic injection molding, assembly, and testing services. Press capacity ranges from 25 to 3,300 tons, supporting projects from prototype through high-volume production. The company employs more than 1,200 people across its manufacturing, technical, and sales facilities, and offers design assistance, product development, material evaluation, and supply-chain management including third-party sourcing.

Revere serves global customers across a range of industries, though specific sectors are not listed. Its marketing emphasizes metal-to-plastic conversion, augmented engineering support, and the consolidation of multiple suppliers into a single logistics partner.

The company was founded to improve the global competitive position of its customers. Its stated differentiator is a “Flexible Thinking, Flexible Design, Flexible Delivery” framework, backed by multiple locations and redundant press space to prevent supply interruptions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Assembly", "Testing", "Design assistance", "Product development", "Material evaluation", "Supply chain management", "Third-party sourcing"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses (25\u20133,300 tons)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Flexible Thinking, Flexible Design, Flexible Delivery framework", "Multiple locations with redundant press capacity", "Top 100 plastic injection molder for 25+ years", "Over 1,200 employees across manufacturing, technical, and sales facilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Novi, Michigan -> /about", "Facility in Ankeny, Iowa -> db", "Over 50 years experience in plastics manufacturing -> /about", "Top 100 injection molders for 25+ years -> /about", "Employs more than 1,200 people -> /about, db", "Press capacity 25\u20133,300 tons -> /about", "Capabilities: injection molding, assembly, testing, design, product development, material evaluation, supply chain management, third-party sourcing -> /about, /", "Founded to improve customers'' global competitive position -> /about, db", "Flexible Thinking, Design, Delivery framework -> /, /about", "Multiple locations and redundant press space -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Revere Plastics Systems\u2019 manufacturing capabilities include value-add plastic injection molding, assembly and testing", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "more than 1,200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='revere-plastics-systems-ankeny' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='RevoluSun Solar is a locally owned and operated solar installation company headquartered in Boise, Idaho. The company serves all of Idaho, Washington, and Oregon from its Mountain States division.

The firm provides full-service solar and energy storage installation for residential and commercial customers. Its offerings include rooftop and ground-mounted solar panel systems, Tesla Solar Roof installations, battery storage using Tesla Powerwall, Sonnen, FranklinWH, and Enphase products, and EV charger installation with Tesla Wall Connector and SPAN Drive equipment. RevoluSun manages the entire process from energy assessment and system design through permitting, inspection, and utility interconnection. To date, the company has completed over 10,000 installations across the Pacific Northwest.

RevoluSun works with homeowners, businesses, and property owners seeking grid resilience and energy independence. Its residential clients include households adding solar, backup batteries, and EV charging, while commercial projects range from small businesses to larger facilities. The company’s project portfolio spans Idaho, eastern Washington, and Oregon, with installations tailored to the region’s climate and utility requirements.

The company emphasizes its Tesla Certified Energy Installer status and a design approach built for the Pacific Northwest’s specific weather and energy patterns. Its stated mission is “building the future of energy by taking care of people and always doing the right thing,” focusing on local expertise, durable products, and seamless project management.', certifications=ARRAY['Tesla Certified Energy Installer']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar panel installation (rooftop and ground mount)", "Tesla Solar Roof installation", "Battery energy storage installation (Tesla Powerwall, Sonnen, FranklinWH, Enphase)", "EV charger installation (Tesla Wall Connector, SPAN Drive)", "Energy assessment and consultation", "System design and engineering", "Permitting and inspection management", "Utility interconnection coordination"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Tesla Powerwall", "Tesla Solar Roof", "Tesla Wall Connector", "SPAN Drive EV Chargers", "Sonnen Battery", "FranklinWH", "Enphase"], "volume": "Over 10,000 installations completed across the Pacific Northwest", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Tesla Certified Energy Installer for Idaho and Eastern Washington", "Over 10,000 residential and commercial installations completed across the Pacific Northwest", "Locally owned and operated since 2009 with offices in Boise, Coeur d\u2019Alene, and Hawaii", "Systems designed specifically for Pacific Northwest climate and utility requirements", "Full-service installation including permitting, inspections, and utility coordination"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 -> db", "Headquarters Boise, Idaho -> db", "Locally owned and operated -> db description", "Services: solar panel installation, Tesla Powerwall, Tesla Solar Roof, EV charging -> db description", "Tesla Certified Energy Installer -> website /", "Over 10,000 installations completed -> website /", "Offices in Boise (2019), Coeur d''Alene (2022), flagship Hawaii -> website /", "Serves Idaho, Washington, Oregon -> website /", "Battery brands: Tesla Powerwall, Sonnen, FranklinWH, Enphase -> website /", "EV charger brands: Tesla Wall Connector, SPAN Drive -> website /", "Full-service including permitting, inspections -> website /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We specialize in residential and commercial solar panel installation, Tesla Powerwall battery storage, Tesla Solar Roof, and EV charging.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/revolusunidaho/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='revolusun-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Revolution Performance Fabrics operates from Kings Mountain, North Carolina, where it has woven performance upholstery fabrics since launching in 2014 as a brand under STI Fabrics — a mill that has been producing textiles in the region since 1964.

The mill designs and weaves its fabrics using Olefin yarn and upcycled fibers, producing stain-resistant, bleach-cleanable materials that are free of PFAS, formaldehyde, heavy metals, phenols, phthalates, and flame retardants. The product range includes jacquards, solids, chenilles, and machine-washable options for both indoor and outdoor applications, all manufactured at the Kings Mountain facility.

The fabrics serve residential furniture makers, outdoor furniture manufacturers, interior designers, and drapery workrooms. Revolution’s trade program caters to members of ASID, IDS, and VRD, offering preferred pricing and dedicated support. Customer reviews highlight use cases such as reupholstering patio furniture and specifying fabrics for client projects, with the Heritage Collection — tailored stripes, plush chenille, and textured wovens — cited as a recent addition.

The brand was created to demonstrate that high-performance upholstery does not require “forever chemicals.” By eliminating PFAS and other hazardous substances while maintaining durability and cleanability, Revolution positions its PFAS-free construction as a safer choice for homes with children and pets.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Weaving", "Textile design", "Performance fabric manufacturing", "Stain-resistant fabric production", "Bleach-cleanable fabric production", "PFAS-free manufacturing", "Upcycled fiber processing", "Custom fabric collections", "Trade account services"], "industries": ["Residential upholstery", "Outdoor furniture", "Interior design", "Drapery and window treatments", "Contract furnishings", "Trade professionals (designers, upholsterers, makers)"], "materials": ["Olefin yarn", "Upcycled fibers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["PFAS-free performance fabrics with no chemical finishes", "Bleach-cleanable and stain-resistant without PFAS", "Woven with Olefin yarn and upcycled fibers in North Carolina", "Free of formaldehyde, heavy metals, phenols, phthalates, and flame retardants", "Comprehensive warranty on all fabrics"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 as part of STI Fabrics (mill since 1964) -> db and /", "Headquarters in Kings Mountain, North Carolina -> db and /about", "Woven with Olefin yarn and upcycled fibers -> /about", "PFAS-free, no chemical treatments -> /about and /", "Stain-resistant, bleach-cleanable, machine washable -> /", "Indoor and outdoor upholstery fabrics -> /", "Trade program for ASID, IDS, VRD members -> /", "Heritage Collection: tailored stripes, plush chenille, textured wovens -> /", "Comprehensive warranty -> /", "Free shipping over $100 -> /", "Customer reviews for outdoor furniture reupholstery -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Revolution Performance Fabrics designs and weaves performance 