UPDATE companies SET description='Ritec Inc. is based in Warwick, Rhode Island, and was formed in 1988 by Gary Petersen and Bruce Chick. The founders, who together brought more than 90 years of experience in ultrasonic instrumentation, set out to develop sophisticated computer-controlled instruments for the rapidly expanding field of ultrasonic non-destructive evaluation (NDE) of materials.

The company designs and manufactures complete computer-controlled ultrasonic systems — including its RAM and SNAP product lines — as well as single-function instruments and accessories. A carefully controlled production environment supports a modular product architecture, and the company notes that more than half of all sales involve some degree of custom modification to meet specific application requirements.

Ritec serves customers in aerospace, materials research, government laboratories, and industrial NDE. Its client roster includes collaborations with NASA, the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST), Johns Hopkins University, the University of Osaka, and private firms such as EMAT Ultrasonics and Matec Applied Sciences. These relationships have produced joint publications and award-winning technical papers.

Ritec’s stated philosophy centers on close collaboration with users during product definition, resulting in instruments that remain at the forefront of technology. Long-standing agreements — including a CRADA with NIST spanning more than five years and a memorandum of agreement with NASA — underpin ongoing instrument upgrades. The company also offers an eight-hour remote training program to help customers maximize the capability of their RAM or SNAP systems.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Ultrasonic instrumentation design", "Computer-controlled system manufacturing", "Custom modification and special orders", "Modular system design", "Remote training (8-hour program)", "Non-destructive evaluation (NDE) instrumentation"], "industries": ["Ultrasonic non-destructive evaluation (NDE)", "Aerospace", "Materials testing", "Research and development", "Government laboratories"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["RAM system", "SNAP system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["More than 50% of sales involve special modification", "Modular configuration for flexibility and upgradability", "CRADA with NIST for over five years and MOA with NASA", "Eight-hour remote training program for RAM/SNAP systems", "Combined 90+ years of founder experience in ultrasonic instrumentation"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 by Gary Petersen and Bruce Chick -> /about-us", "Located at 60 Alhambra Road Suite 5, Warwick, RI 02886 -> /", "Develops computer-controlled ultrasonic instrumentation for NDE -> /about-us", "Offers RAM and SNAP systems, single-function instruments, accessories -> /, /about-us", "More than 50% of sales involve special modification -> /about-us", "Modular configuration for flexibility and upgradability -> /about-us", "Collaborations with NIST, NASA, universities -> /about-us", "CRADA with NIST for more than five years, MOA with NASA -> /about-us", "Leadership: Michael A. Ragosta CEO, Thomas J. Grimsley II President, Michael L. Ficocelli VP, Gary L. Petersen Board Member -> /about-us", "Remote training program (8-hour) for RAM/SNAP systems -> /", "Combined 90+ years of experience in ultrasonic instrumentation -> /about-us", "Quality: sophisticated product line and carefully controlled production environment -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "RITEC prides itself in having developed both a very sophisticated product line and a carefully controlled production environment that precludes compromised instrument performance.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ritec-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ritronics Inc was established in 2011 in Warwick, Rhode Island, to serve the aerospace, defense, and transportation sectors with ruggedized power supplies.

The company designs and manufactures standard COTS and custom AC/DC and DC/DC power supplies ranging from 36 W to 1,000 W, built to withstand extreme temperatures, shock, vibration, and EMI‑dense environments. Its engineering team handles requirements analysis, topology selection, prototype development, design validation, and environmental and EMI/EMC test support, scaling to production with full traceability. Ritronics also provides third‑party logistics services — procurement, kitting, warehousing, and assembly — through its sister company, Calgreg Electronics.

Ritronics serves defense primes, program managers, and design engineers across aerospace, defense, and transportation markets. Its products are qualified to MIL‑STD‑461G for electromagnetic compatibility and meet FCC Part 15 Class B and CISPR 22.2 Class A requirements, supporting programs with decades‑long lifecycles.

The firm emphasizes domestic engineering and manufacturing oversight, direct engineer‑to‑engineer access without call centers or distributors, and standards‑mapped documentation to streamline qualification. It was founded to solve power problems that off‑the‑shelf suppliers won’t touch, offering long‑lifecycle support for programs measured in decades rather than product cycles.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR Registered','NIST 800-171 Certified','ISO 9001:2015','MIL-STD-461G','MIL-STD-461F','DFARS Cyber Security Requirements']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom AC/DC and DC/DC power supply design", "Requirements analysis and topology selection", "Prototype development and design validation", "Environmental and EMI/EMC test support", "Scalable production with full traceability", "Qualification testing and documentation support", "3PL services (procurement, kitting, warehousing, assembly)"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Transportation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["30+ years of defense and aerospace power electronics experience", "Domestic engineering and manufacturing oversight", "Direct engineering access \u2014 no call centers or distributors", "Standards\u2011mapped documentation for qualification support", "Long\u2011lifecycle support for decade\u2011scale programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2011 in Warwick, Rhode Island -> /about", "Primary focus: design and manufacture of ruggedized power supplies -> /about", "Product range 36W to 1,000W, COTS and custom -> /about", "30+ years defense/aerospace power electronics experience -> /", "Domestic engineering and manufacturing oversight -> /", "Direct engineering access, no call centers -> /", "Standards-mapped documentation for qualification -> /", "Long-lifecycle support for decade-scale programs -> /", "Certifications: ITAR, NIST 800-171, ISO 9001:2015, MIL-STD-461G/F, DFARS -> /about", "Industries served: Aerospace, Defense, Transportation -> /about", "3PL services via sister company Calgreg Electronics -> /about", "Qualified to MIL-STD-461G, FCC Part 15 Class B, CISPR 22.2 Class A -> /", "Headquarters: Warwick, Rhode Island -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "RITRONICS'' primary focus is the design and manufacture of ruggedized power supplies for Aerospace, Defense, and Transportation applications.", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ritronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Riverton Sheet Metal Works, Inc. was founded in 1919 in Riverton, Wyoming, during the Prohibition era. The company remains family-owned, tracing its roots to a founder known as "F.B.," who reportedly built copper stills to support his family. That early ingenuity established a tradition of custom metalwork that continues today.

The firm operates as a full-service HVAC contractor and sheet metal fabricator. It sells and installs residential and commercial heating and cooling equipment from brands such as Lennox, York, Bosch, Aprilaire, Rinnai, and WaterFurnace, including geothermal systems. In-house fabrication is performed on a plasma computer-operated table, producing custom ductwork, fittings, and other sheet metal components. The company also supplies humidifiers, ventilation insulation, and parts, and uses proprietary sizing software to tailor equipment to each job.

Customers include homeowners and commercial builders seeking HVAC installation, replacement, or custom sheet metal work. The company serves the renewable energy and geothermal markets, and its product lines carry Energy Star ratings. Past installations span residential and commercial projects throughout the region.

Riverton Sheet Metal distinguishes itself with a "if you can draw it, we can probably build it" approach to custom fabrication, combining decades-old craftsmanship with modern plasma cutting and digital sizing tools. The family-owned structure emphasizes direct customer service and after-sale support.', certifications=ARRAY['ENERGY STAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet metal fabrication", "Plasma cutting", "Ductwork fabrication", "Custom fittings fabrication", "HVAC equipment installation", "HVAC equipment service", "Geothermal system installation", "Humidifier installation", "Ventilation insulation", "Parts supply", "Custom equipment sizing", "Renewable energy system installation"], "industries": ["Residential HVAC", "Commercial HVAC", "Geothermal", "Renewable Energy", "Energy Star"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Plasma computer-operated table", "Proprietary sizing software"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom sheet metal fabrication (\"if you can draw it, we can probably build it\")", "Plasma computer-operated table for ductwork and fittings", "Proprietary software for custom equipment sizing", "Family-owned since 1919", "Energy Star rated product lines"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1919 -> db", "Headquarters Riverton, Wyoming -> db", "Family-owned -> page \"/\"", "Founder ''ole F.B.'' built copper stills -> page \"/\"", "Custom sheet metal fabrication (''if you can draw it, we can probably build it'') -> page \"/\"", "Plasma computer-operated table for ductwork and fittings -> page \"/\"", "Proprietary sizing software for custom equipment fit -> page \"/\"", "HVAC equipment brands: Lennox, York, Bosch, Aprilaire, Rinnai, WaterFurnace -> page \"/\"", "Geothermal systems offered -> page \"/\"", "Energy Star rated products -> page \"/\" and certifications db", "Good Housekeeping Seal of Approval for Armstrong Air -> page \"/\"", "Residential and commercial service -> page \"/\"", "Humidifiers, parts, ventilation insulation supplied -> page \"/\""], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our plasma, computer operated, table allows us to fabricate ductwork, fittings and more.", "founded_year": "1919", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='riverton-sheet-metal-works-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Riveted Woodworking & Design operates from a shop in Bristol, Rhode Island. The business was founded by Althea Tower, who turned a passion for creating into a custom woodworking venture after years of redoing vintage furniture. Althea, who has a background in sewing and fashion design, describes herself as the woman who dared to dream big. In late 2020, her husband Jason officially joined as a partner, making it a family-owned, woman-led small business.

The company specializes in custom built-in cabinetry and accent or feature walls for residential and small-business clients. All work—design, material selection, cutting, sanding, assembly, and installation—is performed in-house by the two-person team in their Bristol shop. They work with real wood, including hardwoods and reclaimed lumber, producing one-of-a-kind pieces that showcase the natural imperfections of the material.

Riveted serves homeowners and small businesses across southeastern New England. Projects range from mudroom organization systems and home office built-ins to decorative shiplap feature walls that add texture to living spaces. The shop''s portfolio includes both residential and light commercial installations.

Althea emphasizes a hands-on, end-to-end experience: every piece is touched by her hands from concept to completion, and the firm prides itself on delivering not just a product but a personal customer journey. The business was honored with a Best of Rhode Island award for Custom-Made Signs, reflecting its commitment to craftsmanship and client satisfaction.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom built-in cabinetry", "Accent/feature walls", "Design and planning", "Handcrafted woodworking", "Installation services"], "industries": ["Residential", "Small business commercial"], "materials": ["Real wood", "Hardwoods", "Reclaimed woods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All design, fabrication, and installation handled in-house by a two-person team", "Every piece handcrafted in their Bristol, RI shop using real wood and reclaimed lumber", "Full-service workflow from design through installation", "Woman-owned, family-run small business with hands-on owner involvement"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bristol, Rhode Island -> /", "Owner: Althea Tower -> /", "Team of two -> /", "Services: custom built-in cabinetry, accent walls -> /", "Design through installation in-house -> /", "Handcrafted, real wood, hardwoods, reclaimed woods -> /about", "Jason joined end of 2020 -> /about", "Award: Best of Rhode Island for Custom-Made Signs -> /about", "Woman-owned, small business, family-owned -> /about", "Founded by Althea after vintage furniture redo -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We build everything in house, in our shop in Bristol, Rhode Island, making each piece truly custom.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "2", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned", "Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='riveted-woodworking-design' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Roanoke Electronic Controls (REC) operates from Roanoke, Alabama, where it has delivered custom electronic solutions for over 25 years. The company was established as a U.S.-based manufacturer dedicated to the design and production of quality electronic controls, offering a turn-key service that takes a concept through design, prototyping, and production.

REC provides full-spectrum engineering and manufacturing under one roof. Its in-house capabilities span schematic design, PCB layout, firmware and embedded software development, and mobile app creation for connected products. On the production side, the facility runs automated SMT assembly with two pick-and-place machines, leaded and lead-free wave soldering, selective soldering, through-hole insertion, automated conformal coating (acrylic, silicone, urethane, epoxy), AOI inspection, and a dedicated BGA/QFP rework station. Every board receives 100% electrical testing. The shop supports prototype runs of 5–25 units through production volumes of 10,000+ units, with a sweet spot in the 500–1,000 unit range.

The company serves a range of industries including outdoor cooking (controllers for brands such as Blaz’n Grill Works and Pitts & Spitts), sports timing (electronics for Victory Game Clocks’ wireless scoreboards and play clocks), alternative energy, industrial monitoring, and fitness equipment. Its Navy-certified soldering expertise also makes it a candidate for military and defense-adjacent programs. Customers include startups and OEMs that need direct engineering access throughout the product lifecycle.

REC emphasizes several differentiators: all engineering is performed in-house by the same team that oversees manufacturing, eliminating handoffs; the quality system is registered to ANSI/ISO 9001:2015 with full traceability; manufacturing is 100% U.S.-based, avoiding overseas delays; and customers work directly with engineers rather than sales intermediaries. The firm also highlights its military-grade soldering capability and true turn-key partnership from napkin sketch to production run.', certifications=ARRAY['ANSI/ISO 9001:2015','MIL-I-46058C','IPC-CC-830B','IPC standards (PCB fabrication)','Navy-certified soldering']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Schematic design", "PCB layout (up to 10+ layers, rigid/flex/rigid-flex/aluminum substrate)", "Firmware/embedded systems development (multi-processor architectures, OTA updates)", "Mobile app development (iOS/Android)", "Cloud-connected firmware update systems", "Automated SMT assembly (2 pick-and-place machines)", "Leaded and lead-free wave soldering", "Selective soldering", "Through-hole assembly (axial, radial, DIP insertion)", "Automated conformal coating (acrylic, silicone, urethane, epoxy)", "AOI inspection", "BGA/QFP rework", "100% electrical testing", "System integration & assembly", "PC-based product testing", "Custom packaging & labeling", "DFM review (free with PCB quote)", "UL/FCC/CSA/CE test coordination", "Environmental testing coordination", "Failure analysis", "Test fixture development", "Materials management & strategic supplier agreements"], "industries": ["Outdoor cooking", "Sports timing", "Alternative energy", "Industrial monitoring", "Fitness equipment", "Military/defense"], "materials": ["FR-4", "High-Tg FR-4", "Rogers", "Polyimide", "Aluminum substrate"], "equipment": ["2 pick-and-place machines", "Leaded wave soldering", "Lead-free wave soldering", "Selective soldering", "Automated conformal coating system", "AOI inspection", "BGA/QFP rework station"], "volume": "Prototype runs (5-25 units) through production volumes (10,000+ units); sweet spot 500-1,000 units", "lead_time": "Prototype assembly 1-3 weeks; production runs 3-6 weeks standard, expedited options available", "tolerances": "4-6 mil min trace width, 8-10 mil min drill, 0.5-3oz copper, 0.4-2.4mm board thickness", "built_on": ["All engineering (hardware, PCB layout, firmware, software) performed in-house by one team", "ANSI/ISO 9001:2015 registered quality management system with full traceability", "100% U.S.-based design, engineering, and manufacturing under one roof in Alabama", "True turn-key partner from concept through design, prototyping, testing, manufacturing, and ongoing support", "Navy-certified soldering expertise with 100% electrical testing on every board"], "facts_used": ["Location: Roanoke, Alabama -> /", "25+ years experience -> /capabilities", "Turn-key design through production -> /", "In-house engineering (hardware, PCB layout, firmware, software, apps) -> /capabilities", "Automated SMT with 2 pick-and-place machines -> /capabilities", "Wave soldering (leaded/lead-free), selective soldering -> /capabilities", "Through-hole insertion -> /capabilities", "Automated conformal coating (4 coating types) -> /capabilities", "AOI inspection, BGA/QFP rework -> /capabilities", "100% electrical testing -> /capabilities", "Prototype 5-25 units, production 10,000+ units -> /capabilities", "Lead times: prototype 1-3 weeks, production 3-6 weeks -> /capabilities", "PCB specs: up to 10+ layers, rigid/flex/rigid-flex, materials -> /capabilities", "ISO 9001:2015 registered -> /", "Navy-certified soldering -> /", "MIL-I-46058C & IPC-CC-830B compliant coating -> /capabilities", "Outdoor cooking industry (Blaz''n Grill Works, Pitts & Spitts) -> /", "Sports timing (Victory Game Clocks) -> /", "Alternative energy mentioned -> /", "Industrial monitors & fitness equipment -> /capabilities", "Direct engineer access, no sales middlemen -> /", "100% US-based manufacturing -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All assembly is performed in-house at our facility in Roanoke, Alabama.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='roanoke-electronic-controls' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
