UPDATE companies SET description='The company supplies the Americas under the ACRYLITE® and ACRYMID® trademarks, while its European, Asian, African and Australian markets are served under the PLEXIGLAS® and PLEXIMID® brands.

The company produces a complete range of PMMA-based standard, impact-modified and special molding compounds. Its Bay City, Texas facility runs the world’s first full-scale industrial operation of the proprietary LiMA technology for methyl methacrylate (MMA) production. Processes include injection compression molding and mold-in-color compounding, which eliminates a separate coating step. The global workforce numbers approximately 2,700 employees.

Roehm serves the automotive, electronics, construction and medical technology industries. In automotive, Volkswagen and its supplier Magna use colored PLEXIGLAS® molding compounds for mold-in-color rear spoilers on the ID. Buzz. Construction and outdoor markets use ACRYLITE® SunResist capstock for window profiles, decking, furniture and façades. The company also supplies medical-grade methacrylate materials.

Roehm emphasizes decarbonization through its methacrylate Verbund. PLEXIGLAS® proTerra grades incorporate mechanically recycled PMMA or sustainably certified raw materials. Mold-in-color manufacturing cuts emissions by avoiding energy-intensive coating. The ACRYLITE® SunResist capstock extends product life in high-exposure outdoor applications.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["MMA production via LiMA technology", "PMMA molding compound manufacturing", "Injection compression molding", "Mold-in-color compounding", "Capstock extrusion (ACRYLITE\u00ae SunResist)", "Recycled content compounding (proTerra)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Electronics", "Construction", "Medical technology", "Outdoor building products", "Recreational components"], "materials": ["PMMA (polymethyl methacrylate)", "MMA (methyl methacrylate)", "Impact-modified PMMA", "Special molding compounds", "Recycled PMMA", "Sustainably certified raw materials", "ACRYLITE\u00ae SunResist capstock material"], "equipment": ["LiMA technology plant", "Injection compression molding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary LiMA technology for MMA production at full industrial scale", "Mold-in-color compounds eliminate coating, reducing carbon emissions", "PLEXIGLAS\u00ae proTerra grades with recycled or certified sustainable content", "ACRYLITE\u00ae SunResist capstock for durable outdoor applications", "Integrated global methacrylate Verbund from monomer to molding compound"], "facts_used": ["Company description and trademarks -> db", "Headquarters location -> db", "Employee count -> db", "LiMA technology at Bay City plant -> homepage", "Mold-in-color for Volkswagen ID. Buzz -> homepage", "ACRYLITE\u00ae SunResist launch -> homepage", "PLEXIGLAS\u00ae proTerra recycled content -> homepage", "Industries served (automotive, electronics, construction, medical) -> homepage", "MMA production via LiMA -> homepage", "Injection compression molding mentioned -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "R\u00d6HM is a worldwide manufacturer of PMMA products sold under the PLEXIGLAS\u00ae and PLEXIMID\u00ae trademarks on the European, Asian, African and Australian continents and under the ACRYLITE\u00ae and ACRYMID\u00ae trademarks in the Americas.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "2700", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='roehm-america-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rogue Industries operates from Standish, Maine, where it was founded in 2007. The company began with a single product: a front-pocket wallet contoured to match the curve of a pocket, slim enough to go unnoticed and secured against theft.

From that original wallet, Rogue Industries expanded into a full line of leather goods, all manufactured in its Maine facility.

The brand sells directly to consumers through its e-commerce site and has partnered with technology companies such as Tile to integrate Bluetooth tracking into a wallet model.

Rogue Industries emphasizes fit, comfort, and durability as its founding principles. It backs its products with a two-year guarantee and offers free U.S. shipping on orders over $75, positioning its Maine-made goods as a long-term alternative to disposable accessories.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Leather goods design", "Leather cutting and stitching", "Wallet manufacturing", "Product development"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Leather", "Premium leather"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Curved, pocket-contoured wallet design", "Two-year product guarantee", "Made in Maine since 2007", "Premium leathers that age well"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2007 -> db", "Headquartered in Standish, Maine -> db", "Manufactures front pocket wallets and leather goods -> /", "Products made in Maine -> /", "Offers 2-year guarantee -> /", "Free shipping on orders $75+ -> /", "Collaboration with Tile on Wallet Tracker -> db", "Over 5,000 reviews -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We built a wallet that actually fits... From that one wallet, we developed a full line of well-made leather goods", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rogue-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rogue Wear by Southern Oregon Embroidery operates from Central Point, Oregon, where it runs a brick-and-mortar storefront The family-owned business traces its origins to a home-based embroidery shop in nearby Medford, started more than a decade ago by the founding family. Their youngest son, Mateo, began sketching designs after a family trip to Texas sparked the idea of creating Oregon-themed apparel.

The company produces its own Rogue Wear clothing line—including overalls, cardigans, hats, and camp goods—and also stocks merchandise from other independent Pacific Northwest brands such as Sendero Provisions. While the business began with contract embroidery for local schools and businesses, it has since expanded into retail, opening its first storefront in February 2017 and moving to a larger space in November 2021. The shop is open Tuesday through Saturday and offers in-person and online sales.

Rogue Wear serves outdoor enthusiasts, campers, and tourists seeking regionally inspired apparel, as well as local organizations that previously ordered custom embroidery. Its customer base includes both walk-in retail shoppers and online buyers across the Pacific Northwest.

