_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='royal-metals-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Royal Plastics, Inc. operates from a 46,000-square-foot facility in Brookings, South Dakota. The company was started in 1978 by Arlen and Jane Rosvold and remains family-owned; today it is held by their children, Michael Peterson and Renee Novak, with the next generation represented by Thomas Peterson as assistant vice president and production manager. The business moved into its current plant in March 1999.

As a custom injection molder of thermoplastics, Royal Plastics runs 15 molding machines ranging from 50 to 300 tons, six of which are all-electric. The shop produces parts from small gram weights up to two pounds, maintaining over 1,300 active part numbers for more than 200 customers across the United States and Canada. A full-service tool room handles mold maintenance, new mold construction, and engineering changes, while an in-house engineering team uses AutoCAD and SolidWorks for mold and part design. Prototyping is supported by a Fortus 250mc 3D printer (10×10×12 in. build envelope, ABSplus-P430 material, ±0.0095 in. accuracy). Quality control relies on a Keyence IM-6120 image dimension system (±2 µm accuracy) and a Mitutoyo QM-Height 600 gauge, backed by a dedicated maintenance program.

The company serves the window and door industry—where it has 40 years of experience—and the after-market automotive sector, among other markets. Its customer base spans OEMs and tier suppliers in both the U.S. and Canada.

Royal Plastics emphasizes a problem-solving culture (“we like problems”) and cites four guiding principles: putting the customer first, imposing no resin restrictions, maintaining dependable quality, and reducing costs. These differentiators are reinforced by on-site mold storage, stocking programs, and design assistance from concept through production.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom injection molding", "Mold design and engineering (AutoCAD, SolidWorks)", "Mold building and maintenance", "Mold storage", "Part design assistance", "Prototyping (FDM 3D printing with Fortus 250mc)", "Quality inspection (Keyence IM-6120, Mitutoyo QM-Height 600)", "Production molding (50\u2013300 ton, all-electric and hydraulic)", "Part stocking and release programs", "Preventive maintenance program"], "industries": ["Window and door", "After-market automotive"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics", "ABSplus-P430 (for 3D printing)"], "equipment": ["15 injection molding machines (50\u2013300 ton, 6 all-electric)", "Fortus 250mc 3D printer", "Keyence IM-6120 Image Dimension Measurement System", "Mitutoyo QM-Height 600 Gauge", "AutoCAD and SolidWorks (software)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.0095 in (3D printed prototypes); \u00b12 \u00b5m (Keyence inspection)", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1978 by Arlen and Jane Rosvold -> /about", "Family-owned, now owned by Michael Peterson and Renee Novak -> /about", "Moved into 46,000 sq ft facility in March 1999 -> /about", "15 molding machines ranging 50-300 ton, six all-electric -> /about", "Parts from small gram weights up to two pounds -> /about, /services", "Over 1,300 different items for over 200 customers in US and Canada -> /about", "Full service tool room for mold maintenance, new molds, changes -> /about", "Engineering department uses AutoCAD and SolidWorks -> /about", "Fortus 250mc 3D printer for prototyping (10x10x12 in, ABSplus-P430, \u00b10.0095 in) -> /about", "Quality checks with Keyence IM-6120 (\u00b12 \u00b5m) and Mitutoyo QM-Height 600 -> /about", "Full-time maintenance department -> /about", "Industries: window and door (40 years experience), after-market automotive -> /about, db", "Services: storage, production, stock, design -> /services", "No restrictions on resins -> /", "Four guiding principles: put customer first, no resin restrictions, high quality, reduce costs -> /", "Problem-solving culture (''we like problems'') -> /", "Headquarters: Brookings, South Dakota -> db, /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Royal Plastics, Inc. is a custom injection molder of thermoplastics.", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='royal-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Royal Switchgear Manufacturing Company has operated from Bessemer, Alabama since its founding in 1914. The business is now a brand within Power Grid Components Inc. (PGC), a holding company that also includes Allied Bolt, Elliott, ITEC, Meister, Mid‑Central, Newell, Vizimax and the affiliated company Blackstone.

The company produces a full line of group‑operated and hookstick disconnect switches, utility‑specific designs and substation power connectors.

Royal Switchgear serves the electric power industry, supplying utilities, industrial operators, municipalities and contractors. Its products are deployed in power distribution networks where minimizing downtime and reducing maintenance costs are critical.

