UPDATE companies SET description='SD Concept Engineering, Inc. (SDCE) was founded in 1995 in East Providence, Rhode Island. The company began as SD Concepts, fabricating custom boost kits for GM, Ford, and Mopar vehicles, and has since grown into a full-service high-performance engine and vehicle builder.

Today, SDCE operates a machine shop equipped with manual Bridgeport mills, a manual lathe, and a CNC milling machine, alongside a dedicated engine assembly room. Its core services include engine building, forced induction systems, engine and chassis dyno tuning, custom tubing and exhaust fabrication, fueling, wiring, cooling, and suspension work. The company also produces a line of high-performance parts under the Air/Fuel Innovations (AFI) brand, developed from over 30 years of product development.

SDCE serves the automotive performance aftermarket, focusing on owners and builders of Mopar, GM, and Ford cars and trucks. Projects have included custom intake manifolds, twin-turbo setups for Dakota trucks, and complete engine assemblies for vehicles such as AMC and Ford Mod motors.

