UPDATE companies SET description='SEMPAC is a privately-owned semiconductor packaging company based in Beaverton, Oregon, in the region known as the Silicon Forest. Founded in 2000 by veterans of the integrated circuit assembly industry, the company was created to offer a more reliable and less expensive alternative to the JEDEC-compliant packages then used for device prototyping and testing. The founders leveraged 50 years of combined experience to develop packaging solutions that did not require specialized assembly equipment or complicated storage.

The company designs, develops, and manufactures pre-molded open cavity plastic packages under the Open-Pak™ brand. Its product line spans QFN, QFP, SOIC, and SSOP architectures in body sizes from 3×3 mm to 12×12 mm, lead counts from 8 to 100, and lead pitches of 0.4 mm to 1.0 mm. Packages are molded with green (halogen-free) compounds, plated with gold over nickel for bondability, and conform to JEDEC outlines. SEMPAC also produces B-Stage lids and offers custom package design. All materials are RoHS 3 and REACH compliant.

SEMPAC serves the semiconductor assembly sector, supplying packages for high-frequency RF, optoelectronics, and power devices in both military and commercial applications. Its customers include integrated circuit manufacturers and assembly houses that need prototyping and test packages without the constraints of traditional contract manufacturing. The company emphasizes collaborative partnerships and does not compete with its customers.

SEMPAC differentiates itself through independence—remaining free of conflicts of interest—and a quality culture that includes inspection at every production stage, from raw material validation to final shipment. The company also commits to environmental responsibility, ensuring products are free of heavy metals per RoHS 3 (EU Directive 2015/863), and to ethical labor practices throughout its supply chain.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS 3 (EU Directive 2015/863)','REACH']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Open cavity plastic package molding", "Gold/nickel (Au/Ni) plating", "JEDEC outline compliance", "Custom package design", "B-Stage lid manufacturing", "Quality inspection at every production stage", "RoHS/REACH compliant material sourcing", "Semiconductor package prototyping and test packages", "High-frequency RF package development", "Optoelectronics packaging", "Power device packaging"], "industries": ["Semiconductor packaging", "Integrated circuit assembly", "High frequency RF", "Optoelectronics", "Power devices", "Military applications", "Commercial applications", "Device prototyping and testing"], "materials": ["Green molding compounds (halogen-free)", "Gold/nickel (Au/Ni) plating", "B-Stage lid materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Independently owned, not competing with customers", "Open-Pak\u2122 packages: green molding compounds, Au/Ni plating, JEDEC compliant", "RoHS 3 and REACH compliant materials", "Collaborative custom package design", "Full-stage inspection from raw material to shipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 -> /about", "Privately-owned company in Pacific Northwest / Silicon Forest -> /", "Headquarters in Beaverton, Oregon -> db", "Manufactures open cavity plastic packages (Open-Pak\u2122) -> /", "Packages molded with green molding compounds, plated with Au/Ni, meet JEDEC outlines -> /", "RoHS and REACH compliant materials -> /", "Offers QFN, QFP, SOIC, SSOP architectures -> /, /about", "Serves high frequency RF, optoelectronics, power devices, military and commercial applications -> /about", "Quality focus with inspection at every stage -> /quality", "Environmental compliance with RoHS 3 (EU Directive 2015/863) -> /quality", "Ethical labor practices -> /quality", "Custom package design capability -> /quality", "B-Stage Lids manufacturing -> /about", "50 years combined experience in semiconductor assembly -> /about", "Independently owned, not competing with customers -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SEMPAC, a privately-owned company in the Pacific Northwest / Silicon Forest devoted to the design, development and manufacture of Pre-molded Open Cavity Plastic Packages.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sempac' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SF Cable, Inc. operates from Hayward, California, where it has built over two decades of experience in the cable and connectivity supply business. The company does not disclose a precise founding year or founder names, nor does it state its ownership structure.

The firm functions as a wholesale distributor, stocking a broad range of power cables, data cables, adapters, and connectivity accessories. Its catalog includes HDMI cables, Cat5e and Cat6 patch cords, universal power cords (NEMA 5-15 to C13), extension cords, DB9 serial cables, USB 2.0/3.0/Type-C cables, DisplayPort cables, fiber optic trunk cables, and modular adapters.

The company positions its offering around five stated commitments: a lifetime warranty on all cables and non-electronics products, no minimum orders or restocking fees, 60-day money-back guarantee, free lifetime technical support, and same-day shipping on in-stock items.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO9001','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale distribution of cables and connectivity products", "Same-day order fulfillment", "Technical support", "Inventory stocking of 1,000+ SKUs"], "industries": ["Industry Expertise"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same day shipping if ordered by 1pm PST", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime warranty on all cables and non-electronics products", "No minimum order quantities and no restocking fees", "60-day money-back guarantee", "Free lifetime technical support"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Hayward, California -> db", "20+ years of cable industry expertise -> /", "ISO9001 and ROHS certifications -> db", "Wholesale supplier of power cables, adapters, HDMI, Cat6, power cords, USB, DisplayPort, fiber optic, serial cables -> /", "Same-day shipping if ordered by 1pm PST -> /", "No minimum orders and no restock fee -> /", "Lifetime warranty on all cables and non-electronics products -> /", "60-day money-back guarantee -> /", "Free lifetime tech support -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Wholesale Supplier for Power Cables, Adapters & More", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum orders", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sf-cable-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SK Food Group traces its roots to 1942 when it began as a mobile catering operation in Seattle, Washington. The company, now headquartered in Reno, Nevada, has grown through a series of ownership changes and name transitions—including Don Campbell''s Quality Food Service in 1979 and Stover''s Kitchen in 2004—before selling its catering division in 2006 to focus exclusively on food manufacturing.

Today the company operates nine state-of-the-art facilities across the United States and Canada, employing more than 2,000 associates. Its plants are custom-built for Ready-to-Eat production, featuring motorized conveyor systems, precision slicing lines for meat and cheese, and extensive cold-storage, dry-storage, and dock infrastructure. All locations are USDA or CFIA certified and carry SQF Version 9.1 certification; the Burnsville and Lakeville, Minnesota sites also hold USDA Organic and Gluten-Free certifications.

SK Food Group serves a broad spectrum of foodservice customers, from independent cafes to Fortune 500 brands, supplying handcrafted sandwiches, wraps, flatbreads, burgers, protein snacks, and charcuterie boards. The company also offers private-label development and assembly, working under strict confidentiality agreements to protect client recipes and packaging intellectual property.

The firm emphasizes a hands-on, confidential partnership model, positioning itself as a collaborator that moves from concept to production while maintaining rigorous food-safety standards. Its "Your Imagination, Our Acceleration" tagline reflects a focus on rapid custom development backed by high-capacity automation.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF Version 9.1','USDA Certified','CFIA Certified','USDA Organic','Gluten-Free']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted food assembly", "Meat and cheese slicing", "Motorized conveyor production systems", "Ready-to-Eat (RTE) product manufacturing", "Private label food production", "Custom food development", "Food safety and quality testing", "USDA/CFIA certified processing", "SQF Version 9.1 certified operations", "Warehousing and cold storage", "Dry storage", "Multi-dock shipping and receiving"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Food manufacturing", "Private label food production"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Motorized conveyor systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted assembly by trained associates on motorized conveyor systems", "Precision slicing of meat and cheese to custom thicknesses and weights", "SQF Version 9.1 certification across all facilities", "USDA and CFIA certified, custom-built processing plants with integrated warehousing", "Commitment to customer confidentiality for recipes, packaging, and brand identity"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1942 as mobile catering company in Seattle -> /about", "Headquartered in Reno, Nevada -> db", "Operates 9 facilities across US and Canada -> /about", "Employs more than 2,000 associates -> /about", "SQF Version 9.1 certification -> /capabilities", "USDA and CFIA certified plants -> /capabilities", "Produces Ready-to-Eat products: sandwiches, wraps, snacks, flatbreads, burgers, protein snacks, charcuterie boards -> /about, /capabilities", "Handcrafted assembly with motorized conveyor systems -> /capabilities", "Slicing capabilit