UPDATE companies SET description='Saginaw Bay Plastics Inc. was founded in 1978 in Kawkawlin, Michigan, as a family‑owned business that evolved from a tool and die operation into a specialist in thermoplastic injection molding.

The company operates injection molding machines ranging from 101 to 1,461 tons and offers two‑shot molding, sequential valve gate controls, sub‑assembly, pad printing, hot stamping, and inkjet barcoding. It processes a range of thermoplastics including polycarbonate, ABS, nylons, polyesters, polypropylene, and glass‑ or mineral‑filled grades. Production is supported by in‑house tool repair, dedicated robots, camera vision inspection, end‑of‑arm tooling, and an ERP system (IQMS) with EDI capability. A just‑in‑time inventory program helps customers reduce stock on hand, and an experienced engineering team collaborates on tooling design for maximum quality and efficiency.

Its primary customers are Tier 1 automotive suppliers for interior components such as headliners, armrests, and panels. The firm also serves the agriculture, marine, and commercial sectors.

Saginaw Bay Plastics emphasizes collaboration and forward‑thinking engineering, performing design of experiments, APQP, PFMEA, and PPAP validation before launch to ensure quality parts delivered on time. The company’s motivation is to provide innovative solutions through collaboration and forward thinking, and it prides itself on its employees and on‑time delivery of quality parts.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Molding", "Two-Shot Injection Molding", "Sequential Valve Gate Controls", "Sub Assembly", "Pad Printing", "Hot Stamping", "Inkjet Barcoding", "End of Arm Tooling", "Dedicated Robots", "Camera Vision Systems for auto-inspection", "In-House Tool Repair and Preventative Maintenance", "Dedicated Tool Sources", "Enterprise IQMS (ERP)", "Scheduling / Planning", "Transaction Manager (EDI)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Agriculture", "Marine", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Polycarbonate", "ABS", "Nylon", "Polyester", "Polypropylene", "Glass-filled thermoplastics", "Mineral-filled thermoplastics"], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (101\u20131,461 ton)", "Two-shot injection molding machines", "Dedicated robots", "Camera vision inspection systems", "End-of-arm tooling"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Just\u2011in\u2011time inventory delivery to reduce customer stock", "In\u2011house tool repair and preventative maintenance", "Camera vision systems for automated inspection", "Two\u2011shot injection molding up to 1,461 tons", "Pre\u2011production DOE, APQP, PFMEA, and PPAP validation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1978 -> db", "Family-owned -> /about", "Location Kawkawlin, Michigan -> db and /about", "Transition from tool & die to injection molding -> /about", "Machine sizes 101-1461 Ton -> /about", "JIT inventory program -> /about", "DOE, APQP, PFMEA, PPAP before launch -> /about", "Serves Tier 1 automotive suppliers for interior parts (headliners, armrests, panels) -> /about", "Also serve