UPDATE companies SET description='Sawtooth Wood Products operates from Bellevue, Idaho, in the Wood River Valley. The company traces its roots to Bob Parker, who established the business as a log construction specialist serving Ketchum, Hailey, Sun Valley, and Bellevue. The current owner, a former Boise State Broncos running back who played in the 2007 Fiesta Bowl, took over the company after growing up on his grandparents'' Idaho ranch. He brought a philosophy of optimal performance shaped by athletics and agricultural work.

The firm provides two core services: custom log construction of homes and buildings, and fence installation ranging from residential picket fences to commercial security fencing. Each project is approached as a customized solution, with the team working directly with clients to match specific design and functional requirements.

Customers include homeowners and businesses throughout the Wood River Valley. Examples cited by the company include backyard picket fences for residences and large security fences for commercial properties, as well as one-of-a-kind log homes that reflect the region''s architectural character.

The owner cites his football background — teamwork, perseverance, attention to detail, and handling pressure — as directly applicable to construction craftsmanship. The company emphasizes carrying forward Bob Parker''s legacy, using quality materials and focusing on optimal performance in every detail. The driving force is described as the passion and dedication the team puts into each piece of wood.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Log construction", "Fence installation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Customized solutions for each client", "Legacy of log construction in the Wood River Valley since Bob Parker", "Owner''s high-level athletic background informing attention to detail", "Commitment to optimal performance in materials and craftsmanship", "Service across Ketchum, Hailey, Sun Valley, and Bellevue"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bellevue, Idaho -> db", "Services: log construction and fence installation -> db", "Owner background: former Boise State Broncos running back, 2007 Fiesta Bowl -> /about", "Company taken over from Bob Parker -> /about", "Service areas: Ketchum, Hailey, Sun Valley, Bellevue -> db", "Customized solutions for each customer -> /about", "Commitment to optimal performance and legacy -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "specializes in log construction in Ketchum, Hailey, Sun Valley, and Bellevue, and we take great pride in our ability to create stunning, one-of-a-kind homes and buildings that capture the essence of the Wood River Valley. We are also experts in fence installation", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sawtooth-wood-products-fencing-and-equipment' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='S.A.Y. Plastics Inc. operates a custom injection molding facility in Jacksonville, Texas. The company has been in business for over 30 years, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The plant spans more than 220,000 square feet of production and warehousing space and runs 41 injection molding presses ranging from 75 to 2,000 tons of clamping force. The company processes engineering resins such as ABS, PVC, nylon, polycarbonate, and PPS, along with commodity resins including polyethylene, polypropylene, and polystyrene. Secondary operations cover solvent welding, hot stamping, image transfer, secondary machining, assembly, special packaging, and distribution, plus support for new mold creation and mold modifications. The workforce numbers approximately 150 employees.

S.A.Y. Plastics supplies molded components to the pet products, plumbing, HVAC, and automotive sectors.

