aning, pressed cane, rush, splint -> /", "No painted finishes -> /", "Transparency, visitors welcome -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializes in creating custom handmade furniture from premium solid hardwoods and providing expert furniture repair and furniture refinishing services", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='schanz-furniture-refinishing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Scherer Metals operates from Denver, Colorado, where it was founded in 1896 as Frank Scherer & Sons. The business passed to the Koenig family, which has stewarded the company through multiple generations, maintaining a focus on architectural metal fabrication.

The shop provides custom architectural and decorative metal fabrication, including shearing, punching, bending, polishing, MIG and TIG welding, and patina finishing. On-staff draftsmen and engineers translate concepts into build-ready designs, while project managers oversee complex jobs from start to finish. The facility also handles restoration and repair of existing metal components and stocks finishing materials such as corner guards and kick plates.

Its portfolio includes railings, cladding, furniture, and decorative metalwork, with patina finishes applied using Sculpt Nouveau products, which the company distributes.

The company cites its 129-year history and certified welding staff as key differentiators, emphasizing on-time delivery and the ability to turn client visions into reality. As a distributor of Sculpt Nouveau metal paints, patinas, and clear coats, it offers a single source for both fabrication and specialty finishes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Shearing", "Punching", "Bending", "Polishing", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Design and engineering", "Patina finishing", "Restoration and repair", "Project management", "Architectural metal fabrication", "Decorative metal fabrication", "Finishing materials supply (corner guards, kick plates)", "Distribution of Sculpt Nouveau products"], "industries": ["Architectural metal fabrication", "Decorative metalwork", "Railings", "Cladding", "Furniture", "Patina finishes"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 129 years of continuous operation in architectural metal fabrication", "On-staff draftsmen and engineers produce build-ready designs", "Certified welders qualified for MIG and TIG processes", "Project management service that coordinates complex jobs from start to finish", "Authorized distributor of Sculpt Nouveau metal paints, patinas, and clear coats"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1896 -> /", "Frank Scherer & Sons and Koenig family stewardship -> /", "Location: 1299 E. 58th Avenue, Denver, CO 80216 -> /", "Services: shearing, punching, bending, polishing, MIG/TIG welding, design & engineering, finishing materials, restoration & repair, project management -> /", "Portfolio includes railings, cladding, furniture, decorative metalwork, patina finishes -> /", "Distributor of Sculpt Nouveau Metal Paints, Patinas, Clear Coats and Finishes -> /", "Claim: Colorado''s #1 custom architectural metal fabricator, 129 years experience -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, Scherer Metals stands as Colorado''s #1 custom architectural metal fabricator.", "founded_year": "1896", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='scherer-metals-1299-e-58th-avenue-denver' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Schlotterbeck & Foss Co. has operated from Westbrook, Maine since 1866, when Augustus G. Schlotterbeck and Charles S. Foss opened a prescription apothecary shop. The partners built a reputation for quality handcrafted products and fair dealings, later expanding into patented medicines and flavoring extracts in the 20th century.

Today the company manufactures a range of specialty foods including chef sauces, marinades, condiments, cooking sauces, artisan salsas, spreads, dessert sauces, and dressings. Its core competency lies in product development and proprietary small‑batch manufacturing, using a preparation, cooking, and packaging process designed to retain the shape, texture, and flavor of large‑cut ingredients such as blueberries, corn, mango, and whole garlic cloves. Formulations emphasize organic, non‑GMO, and clean‑label ingredients with no preservatives or artificial colors.

The company serves natural and conventional grocery retailers, club stores, and food‑service operators through private‑label programs and its own branded lines.

Schlotterbeck & Foss traces its differentiation to over 150 years of continuous experience, artisan handcrafting methods, and a focus on ingredient integrity that it says cannot be replicated by competitors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Small-batch manufacturing", "Product development and ideation", "Custom formulation", "Proprietary preparation, cooking and packaging", "Private label production", "Food service supply", "Artisan handcrafting"], "industries": ["Natural grocery retail", "Conventional grocery retail", "Club store retail", "Food service", "Private label specialty foods"], "materials": ["Organic ingredients", "Non-GMO ingredients", "Clean-label ingredients", "Dutch cocoa", "Specialty coffee beans", "Fresh fruits and vegetables", "All-natural seasonings and spices"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary small-batch manufacturing process", "Custom product ideation and development", "Large-cut ingredient retention technology", "Clean-label, no-preservative formulations", "150+ years of continuous operation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1866 as prescription apothecary shop by Augustus G. Schlotterbeck and Charles S. Foss -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Westbrook, Maine -> db", "Produces sauces, condiments, dressings, dessert sauces, salsas, spreads, marinades -> /", "Uses proprietary small-batch manufacturing and custom formulation -> /about-us", "Serves natural, conventional grocery and club store retailers -> /", "Offers private label and food service -> /", "Uses organic, clean-label, non-GMO ingredients -> /about-us", "Proprietary preparation, cooking, packaging process retains ingredient integrity -> /", "Artisan handcrafting methods emphasized -> /about-us", "Over 150 years of experience claimed -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our core competency in product development supports our proprietary small batch manufacturing capabilities, resulting in marquee specialty foods.", "founded_year": "1866", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='schlotterbeck-foss-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Schmidt Equipment & Supply traces its roots to 1943 in St. Louis, Missouri, when Roy Elias Schmidt and Leo Welch founded the Schmidt‑Welch Equipment Company to rebuild and service meat‑processing machinery during World War II. Welch soon sold his share to Schmidt, and the firm became Roy E. Schmidt Sales & Service Co. The business has remained in the Schmidt family for three generations.

Today the company operates as a single‑source distributor and service provider for the meat and food processing sectors. Its product lineup includes hydraulic stuffers, smokehouses, grinders, slicers, band saws, vacuum sealers, tumblers, mixers, injectors, patty molders, batter and breading systems, and a full range of supplies such as casings, seasonings, packaging materials, and cutting tools. A parts department sources components from major brands, and a service team offers scheduled maintenance and emergency after‑hours calls. The operation runs from a facility that houses a test kitchen and demonstration lab, serving customers within a 150‑mile radius of St. Louis across Missouri and Illinois.

The customer base spans commercial meat processors, sausage makers, and food manufacturers producing items such as salami, summer sausage, capicola, mortadella, bologna, and pork rolls.

